    "q-331980": {
      "dom_id": "step-q331980",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t)$",
      "worked_solution": "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\n{x}_{i}^{′}(t)={\\lambda }_{i}{x}_{i}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\lambda }_{i}$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently.  \n\nIn matrix form, a linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ is decoupled if $A$ is a diagonal matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- Systems I and III are decoupled since their corresponding matrices are diagonal.\n\n- System II is *not* decoupled because its matrix is not diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
