    "q-332709": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332709",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-332709-a",
